<Layout
  title="Quick Guide to Using This Site & the World Tipiṭaka"
  description="Interactive Quick Guide to the World Tipiṭaka Edition on tipitaka2500.github.io: volume and book codes, paragraph citations, footnotes, page concordances, edition abbreviations, and Pāḷi pronunciation."
  currentBook="guide"
  lang="en"
>
  <main class="index-page">
    <div class="index-hero">
      <h1>Quick Guide to the World Tipiṭaka &amp; This Website</h1>
      <p>
        How to read canonical citations, navigate the 40 volumes and 88 books, use interactive
        badges and footnotes, cross-reference printed editions, and pronounce Roman and IPA Pāḷi
        (adapted from the <a href="https://www.sajjhaya.org/node/181" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Dhamma Society Quick Guide ↗</a>).
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 1: Keyboard Shortcuts & Site Navigation -->
    <article class="index-card" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
      <h2 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--text-emphasis);">
        1. Quick Navigation &amp; Keyboard Shortcuts
      </h2>
      <div class="verse-grid">
        <div>
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-emphasis);">
            Instant Citation &amp; Book Lookup
          </h3>
          <p style="font-size: 0.92rem;">
            Press <kbd class="quick-jump-kbd">⌘K</kbd> (or <kbd class="quick-jump-kbd">Ctrl+K</kbd>
            / <kbd class="quick-jump-kbd">/</kbd>) anywhere on the site—or click the search button at
            the top of the sidebar—to open the <strong>Quick Jump &amp; Citation Lookup</strong>
            dialog:
          </p>
          <ul style="font-size: 0.92rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
            <li>
              <strong>Jump to an exact paragraph:</strong> Type <code>1V:2</code>,
              <code>18Dh:1</code>, or <code>24Mn:1898</code> and press <kbd class="quick-jump-kbd">Enter</kbd>
              to jump straight to that paragraph in the text.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Find any book:</strong> Type a book code (<code>6D</code>, <code>19Th1</code>,
              <code>40P24</code>) or title (<code>Dhammapada</code>, <code>Mahāvagga</code>,
              <code>Paṭṭhāna</code>).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Search across all 5 indices:</strong> Type any Pāḷi word or phrase to search
              the Word Index, Verses, TOC, or Critical Notes with one click.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Toggle Dictionary Lookup:</strong> Click the <strong>📖 Dictionary Lookup</strong>
              button in the top header bar or sidebar drawer to enable or disable instant on-hover/tap word definitions, grammar symbols, and compound deconstructions.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-emphasis);">
            Reader Keyboard &amp; URL Conventions
          </h3>
          <ul style="font-size: 0.92rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
            <li>
              <kbd class="quick-jump-kbd">Alt + ←</kbd> / <kbd class="quick-jump-kbd">Alt + →</kbd>:
              Navigate to the <strong>Previous</strong> or <strong>Next</strong> canonical section.
            </li>
            <li>
              <kbd class="quick-jump-kbd">Alt + ↑</kbd>: Navigate <strong>Up</strong> to the parent
              section or book index.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Book URL:</strong> <code>/tipitaka/&#123;BookCode&#125;.html</code> (e.g.{' '}
              <a href="/tipitaka/1V.html">/tipitaka/1V.html</a>,{' '}
              <a href="/tipitaka/18Dh.html">/tipitaka/18Dh.html</a>).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Section URL:</strong> <code>/tipitaka/&#123;BookCode&#125;/&#123;SectionPath&#125;.html</code>{' '}
              (e.g. <a href="/tipitaka/1V/1.html">/tipitaka/1V/1.html</a>).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Paragraph Anchor:</strong> <code>#p_&#123;BookCode&#125;_&#123;ParagraphNo&#125;</code>{' '}
              (e.g. <a href="/tipitaka/1V/1.html#p_1V_2">/tipitaka/1V/1.html#p_1V_2</a>).
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Section 2: Anatomy of a Tipitaka Page (Plate 3) -->
    <article class="index-card" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
      <h2 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--text-emphasis);">
        2. Anatomy of a Tipiṭaka Page &amp; Interactive Elements (Plate 3)
      </h2>
      <p>
        In the printed 40-volume World Tipiṭaka Edition, each page displays division numbers,
        paragraph numbers, superscript footnote numbers, and marginal page concordances. On this
        website, the reading view is kept clean and distraction-free while every reference element
        is <strong>interactive</strong>:
      </p>

      <div
        class="tipitaka-content"
        style="padding: 1.15rem 1.35rem; margin: 1rem 0; border: 1px solid var(--primary-color); border-radius: 0.5rem; background-color: var(--badge-light-bg);"
      >
        <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          Live Example from Pārājikapāḷi — Verañjakaṇḍa (<a href="/tipitaka/1V/1.html#p_1V_2">1V:2</a>)
        </div>
        <main>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <span class="division-number" title="Division Number (book_div)">1.</span>
            <span
              class="paragraph-number interactive-badge"
              title="Paragraph Number (1V:2) — Click on any reading page for citation tools"
            >
              2
            </span>
            Tena samayena buddho bhagavā verañjāyaṁ<sup class="footnote-ref"><a href="/tipitaka/1V/1.html#fn-p_1V_2_1">[1]</a></sup>
            viharati naḷerupucimandamūle mahatā bhikkhusaṅghena saddhiṁ pañcamattehi
            bhikkhusatehi. Assosi kho verañjo brāhmaṇo: “samaṇo khalu, bho, gotamo sakyaputto
            sakyakulā pabbajito…”
          </p>
        </main>
      </div>

      <div class="index-table-wrapper">
        <table class="index-table">
          <caption>How Print Reference Elements Map to Interactive Features on This Website</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Element</th>
              <th scope="col">Example</th>
              <th scope="col">What It Means &amp; How to Use It Here</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Division Number Badge</strong></td>
              <td>
                <span
                  style="display: inline-block; padding: 0.25em 0.6em; font-size: 0.78em; font-weight: 700; border-radius: 50rem; background-color: var(--badge-secondary-bg); color: var(--badge-secondary-color);"
                >
                  1.
                </span>
              </td>
              <td>
                Indicates the canonical text division (<em>khandhaka</em>, <em>sutta</em>,
                <em>sikkhāpada</em>, or <em>vatthu</em> number) within the book.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Paragraph Number Badge</strong></td>
              <td>
                <span class="badge-pill">2</span>
              </td>
              <td>
                Indicates the sequential paragraph number within the book (e.g. <code>1V:2</code> or
                <code>1V:0002</code>). <strong>Click any paragraph badge</strong> on a reading page
                to open a popover to <strong>Copy Permalink</strong> (<code>#p_1V_2</code>),{' '}
                <strong>Copy Citation</strong> (<code>1V:2</code>), or open that paragraph in{' '}
                <a href="/concordances.html?book=1V&q=1V%3A0002">Page Concordances</a>,{' '}
                <a href="/notes.html?book=1V&q=1V%3A2">Critical Notes</a>, or{' '}
                <a href="/verses.html?book=1V&q=1V%3A0002">Verses</a>.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Footnote Reference</strong></td>
              <td>
                <code>verañjāyaṁ<sup>[1]</sup></code>
              </td>
              <td>
                Indicates a critical apparatus note in the <em>Tipiṭaka Studies Reference</em>.{' '}
                <strong>Click <code>[1]</code></strong> on any reading page to preview the note in a
                floating card without scrolling to the bottom of the page. Edition abbreviations
                (such as <abbr class="edition-abbr" title="Sīhaḷa (Sri Lankan Edition)">sī</abbr>,{' '}
                <abbr class="edition-abbr" title="Syāmaraṭṭha 1st–3rd Editions">syā1-3</abbr>,{' '}
                <abbr class="edition-abbr" title="Pāḷi Text Society 1st Edition">pā1</abbr>) show
                explanatory tooltips on hover.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Cross-Reference Link</strong></td>
              <td>
                <a href="/tipitaka/24Mn/1/16.html#p_24Mn_1898">24Mn:1898</a>,{' '}
                <a href="/tipitaka/1V/1/2/1.html#p_1V_28">1V.15/1</a>
              </td>
              <td>
                Cross-references inside footnotes (both colon-style <code>Book:Paragraph</code> and
                dot/slash-style <code>Book.Division/Paragraph</code>) are hyperlinked directly to
                the target page and paragraph on this website.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Page Concordances</strong></td>
              <td>
                <code>1B2, 1C1, 1Ch¹1, 3P¹1, 1S1, 87V1</code>
              </td>
              <td>
                In the printed books, marginal codes show the volume and page in other Tipiṭaka
                editions (e.g. <code>1B2</code> = Vol. 1, Page 2 of the Buddhajayantī Edition;{' '}
                <code>3P¹1</code> = Vol. 3, Page 1 of the PTS 1st Edition). On this website, click
                any paragraph badge or visit <a href="/concordances.html">Page Concordances</a> to
                filter and search all 164,784 concordance mappings.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Pāḷi Word Index</strong></td>
              <td>
                <code>aggisālā [aggisālā] — 15</code>
              </td>
              <td>
                In the printed volumes, the end-of-volume index lists every word’s headword, IPA
                pronunciation, and occurrences. On this website, visit the{' '}
                <a href="/words.html?q=aggisala">Pāḷi Word Index</a> to search all 146,693 headwords
                across all 88 books with clickable occurrence badges.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Pāḷi Word (Dictionary Lookup)</strong></td>
              <td>
                <code>bhagavā</code> → <span class="badge-code">🚹①⨀ bhagavant</span><br />
                <code>evamme</code> → <span class="badge-code">evaṃ + me</span>
              </td>
              <td>
                When <strong>Dictionary Lookup</strong> is active (toggled via <code>📖</code>), hover any word
                on desktop (or tap on mobile) in the canonical text to display an instant popover with its
                lemma, English meaning, textbook grammar notation symbols, and compound/sandhi deconstruction pills.
                Click any constituent pill to look up that component word.
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Section 3: Pāḷi Grammar Dictionary Lookup & Notation Guide -->
    <article class="index-card" id="dict-lookup" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
      <h2 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--text-emphasis);">
        3. Pāḷi Grammar Dictionary Lookup &amp; Notation Guide
      </h2>
      <p>
        The reading view includes a fast, client-side <strong>Pāḷi Grammar Dictionary Lookup</strong> and
        <strong>Compound/Sandhi Deconstructor</strong> derived from the <a href="https://digitalpalidictionary.github.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Digital Pāḷi Dictionary (DPD)</a>.
        When enabled, readers can hover over any Pāḷi word on desktop (or tap on mobile/touch screens) to
        open a popover showing:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Headwords &amp; English Definitions:</strong> Primary meanings, grammatical constructions, and verbal roots (e.g. <code>√bhū + a</code>).</li>
        <li><strong>Pāḷi Word Index Link:</strong> Click <em>Word Index ↗</em> in the popover header to jump directly to the occurrence list and Thai/IPA forms in the <a href="/words.html">Pāḷi Word Index</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Compound &amp; Sandhi Splits:</strong> Complex words are deconstructed into interactive clickable pills (e.g. <code>evamme</code> → <code>evaṃ</code> + <code>me</code>). Clicking any pill navigates to that component word, with a <code>← back</code> button to return.</li>
        <li><strong>Grammatical Inflection Analysis:</strong> Detailed tables classifying part of speech, grammatical category, case usage, and symbolic notation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 style="margin-top: 1.25rem; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text-emphasis);">
        Textbook Grammar Notation Symbols
      </h3>
      <p style="font-size: 0.92rem;">
        To convey grammatical inflections compactly without verbose abbreviations, the dictionary uses visual
        notation symbols from the author’s Pāḷi textbook:
      </p>

      <div class="verse-grid" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        <div class="index-table-wrapper">
          <table class="index-table" style="font-size: 0.88rem;">
            <caption>Noun &amp; Pronoun Declensions (Liṅga, Vibhatti, Vacana)</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Symbol</th>
                <th scope="col">Grammar Category</th>
                <th scope="col">Syntactic Usage</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>🚹</code></td><td>Masculine (Pulliṅga)</td><td>Gender</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>🚺</code></td><td>Feminine (Itthīliṅga)</td><td>Gender</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>🚻</code></td><td>Neuter (Napuṁsakaliṅga)</td><td>Gender</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>⚧️</code></td><td>Any / Common Gender</td><td>Adjectives &amp; Pronouns</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>⨀</code></td><td>Singular (Ekavacana)</td><td>Number</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>⨂</code></td><td>Plural (Bahuvacana)</td><td>Number</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>①</code></td><td>Nominative (Paṭhamā)</td><td>Subject</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>②</code></td><td>Accusative (Dutiyā)</td><td>Object</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>③</code></td><td>Instrumental (Tatiyā)</td><td>by / with</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>④</code></td><td>Dative (Catutthī)</td><td>for / to</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>⑤</code></td><td>Ablative (Pañcamī)</td><td>from</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>⑥</code></td><td>Genitive (Chaṭṭhī)</td><td>of / 's</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>⑦</code></td><td>Locative (Sattamī)</td><td>in / at / on</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>⓪</code></td><td>Vocative (Ālapana)</td><td>Direct address</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>🆎</code></td><td>In Compounds (Samāsa)</td><td>Prefix / Stem form</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <div class="index-table-wrapper">
          <table class="index-table" style="font-size: 0.88rem;">
            <caption>Verb Conjugations &amp; Moods (Ākhyāta, Purisa, Kāla)</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Symbol</th>
                <th scope="col">Grammar Category</th>
                <th scope="col">Tense / Mood / Voice</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>▶️</code></td><td>Present (Vattamānā)</td><td>Action happening now</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>⏭</code></td><td>Future (Bhavissantī)</td><td>Action to come</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>⏮</code></td><td>Aorist (Ajjatanī)</td><td>Past completed action</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>⏯</code></td><td>Optative (Sattamī)</td><td>Potential, wish, advice</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>⏹</code></td><td>Imperative (Pañcamī)</td><td>Command, blessing</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>🔀</code></td><td>Conditional (Kālātipatti)</td><td>Hypothetical condition</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>↩️</code></td><td>Imperfect (Hiyyattanī)</td><td>Past continuous</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>🔄</code></td><td>Perfect (Parokkhā)</td><td>Historical past</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>🟢</code></td><td>Active Voice (Parassapada)</td><td>Subject performs action</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>🔵</code></td><td>Reflexive Voice (Attanopada)</td><td>Subject affected by action</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>👆</code></td><td>1st Person (Uttamapurisa)</td><td>I, we (ahaṁ, mayaṁ)</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>🤘</code></td><td>2nd Person (Majjhimapurisa)</td><td>you (tvaṁ, tumhe)</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>🤟</code></td><td>3rd Person (Paṭhamapurisa)</td><td>he, she, it, they</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tipitaka-content" style="padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 0.5rem; background-color: var(--badge-light-bg); font-size: 0.92rem;">
        <strong>Example Analysis:</strong>
        <ul style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.25rem;">
          <li><code>bhagavā</code> → <code>🚹①⨀(bhagavant)</code>: Masculine nominative singular subject of stem <em>bhagavant</em> ("blessed one, Lord").</li>
          <li><code>deseti</code> → <code>▶️🤟🟢(disa)</code>: Present tense, 3rd person singular, active voice of root <em>√dis</em> ("teaches, explains, expounds").</li>
          <li><code>dhammameva</code> → <code>dhammaṃ + eva</code>: Split into <em>dhammaṃ</em> (<code>🚻②⨀</code>, object "Dhamma") + <em>eva</em> (particle "indeed, truly, only").</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

