    <!-- Section 5: Guide to Pali Pronunciation & Phonetics (Plates 7 & 8) -->
    <article class="index-card" style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
      <h2 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--text-emphasis);">
        5. Guide to Pāḷi Pronunciation: The 41 Pāḷi Sounds (Plates 7 &amp; 8)
      </h2>
      <p>
        According to the ancient <em>Kaccāyana Pāḷi Grammar</em> (<em>Akkharāpādayo ekacattālīsaṁ</em>),
        Pāḷi comprises <strong>41 sounds</strong>: <strong>8 vowels</strong> (<em>sara</em>) and{' '}
        <strong>33 consonants</strong> (<em>vyañjana</em>, divided into 25 classified{' '}
        <em>vagga</em> consonants and 8 unclassified <em>avagga</em> consonants). Both Roman Pāḷi
        and International Phonetic Alphabet (IPA) transcriptions are used side-by-side in our{' '}
        <a href="/words.html">Pāḷi Word Index</a>:
      </p>

      <div class="index-table-wrapper" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        <table class="index-table">
          <caption>The 8 Pāḷi Vowels (Sara) — Short (Lahu) vs. Long (Garu)</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Articulation Place</th>
              <th scope="col">Short Vowel (Lahu — 1 Metre)</th>
              <th scope="col">Long Vowel (Garu — 2 Metres)</th>
              <th scope="col">Pronunciation Note</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Velar (Kaṇṭhaja — Throat)</strong></td>
              <td><code>a</code> &nbsp; <code>[a]</code></td>
              <td><code>ā</code> &nbsp; <code>[aː]</code></td>
              <td>Open vowel as in <em>hut</em> (short) vs. <em>father</em> (long)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Palatal (Tāluja — Hard Palate)</strong></td>
              <td><code>i</code> &nbsp; <code>[i]</code></td>
              <td><code>ī</code> &nbsp; <code>[iː]</code></td>
              <td>Close front vowel as in <em>bit</em> (short) vs. <em>machine</em> (long)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Labial (Oṭṭhaja — Lips)</strong></td>
              <td><code>u</code> &nbsp; <code>[u]</code></td>
              <td><code>ū</code> &nbsp; <code>[uː]</code></td>
              <td>Close back rounded vowel as in <em>put</em> (short) vs. <em>rule</em> (long)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Palato-Velar (Kaṇṭhatāluja)</strong></td>
              <td><code>e</code> (before double consonant)</td>
              <td><code>e</code> &nbsp; <code>[eː]</code></td>
              <td>Naturally long <code>[eː]</code> as in <em>they</em>; short before two consonants (e.g. <em>mettā</em>)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Labio-Velar (Kaṇṭhoṭṭhaja)</strong></td>
              <td><code>o</code> (before double consonant)</td>
              <td><code>o</code> &nbsp; <code>[oː]</code></td>
              <td>Naturally long <code>[oː]</code> as in <em>go</em>; short before two consonants (e.g. <em>bhoggo</em>)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="index-table-wrapper" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        <table class="index-table">
          <caption>The 33 Pāḷi Consonants (Vyañjana) by Place (Ṭhāna) &amp; Manner (Karaṇa) of Articulation (Plate 8)</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Place of Articulation (Ṭhāna)</th>
              <th scope="col">Voiceless Unaspirated (Aghosa Sithila)</th>
              <th scope="col">Voiceless Aspirated (Aghosa Dhanita)</th>
              <th scope="col">Voiced Unaspirated (Ghosa Sithila)</th>
              <th scope="col">Voiced Aspirated (Ghosa Dhanita)</th>
              <th scope="col">Nasal (Nāsikaṭṭhānaja)</th>
              <th scope="col">Avagga (Liquids, Approximants &amp; Fricatives)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Velar (Kaṇṭhaja)</strong></td>
              <td><code>k</code> <code>[k]</code></td>
              <td><code>kh</code> <code>[kʰ]</code></td>
              <td><code>g</code> <code>[g]</code></td>
              <td><code>gh</code> <code>[ɡʱ]</code></td>
              <td><code>ṅ</code> <code>[ŋ]</code></td>
              <td><code>h</code> <code>[ɦ]</code> (Glottal)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Palatal (Tāluja)</strong></td>
              <td><code>c</code> <code>[c]</code></td>
              <td><code>ch</code> <code>[cʰ]</code></td>
              <td><code>j</code> <code>[ɟ]</code></td>
              <td><code>jh</code> <code>[ɟʱ]</code></td>
              <td><code>ñ</code> <code>[ɲ]</code></td>
              <td><code>y</code> <code>[j]</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Post-Alveolar / Retroflex (Muddhaja)</strong></td>
              <td><code>ṭ</code> <code>[ʈ]</code></td>
              <td><code>ṭh</code> <code>[ʈʰ]</code></td>
              <td><code>ḍ</code> <code>[ɖ]</code></td>
              <td><code>ḍh</code> <code>[ɖʱ]</code></td>
              <td><code>ṇ</code> <code>[ɳ]</code></td>
              <td><code>r</code> <code>[ɻ]</code>, &nbsp; <code>ḷ</code> <code>[ɭ]</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Dental (Dantaja)</strong></td>
              <td><code>t</code> <code>[t̪]</code></td>
              <td><code>th</code> <code>[t̪ʰ]</code></td>
              <td><code>d</code> <code>[d̪]</code></td>
              <td><code>dh</code> <code>[d̪ʱ]</code></td>
              <td><code>n</code> <code>[n̪]</code></td>
              <td><code>l</code> <code>[l̪]</code>, &nbsp; <code>s</code> <code>[s̪]</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Bilabial / Labio-Dental (Oṭṭhaja)</strong></td>
              <td><code>p</code> <code>[p]</code></td>
              <td><code>ph</code> <code>[pʰ]</code></td>
              <td><code>b</code> <code>[b]</code></td>
              <td><code>bh</code> <code>[bʱ]</code></td>
              <td><code>m</code> <code>[m]</code></td>
              <td><code>v</code> <code>[ʋ]</code> (Labio-dental)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Niggahīta (Pure Nasal)</strong></td>
              <td colspan="5" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
                Nasalized resonance following a short vowel (<code>aṁ</code>, <code>iṁ</code>, <code>uṁ</code>)
              </td>
              <td><code>ṁ</code> <code>[ã / ŋ]</code></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="index-table-wrapper">
        <table class="index-table">
          <caption>Non-Cluster (Geminate) vs. Cluster Consonants in Pāḷi Pronunciation (Plate 7)</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Non-Cluster Sound (Geminate / Final Arrest)</th>
              <th scope="col">IPA &amp; Syllabic Division</th>
              <th scope="col">Cluster Sound Only (Onset Consonant Cluster)</th>
              <th scope="col">IPA &amp; Syllabic Division</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td lang="pi"><strong>kallaṁ</strong> (กัลล์)</td>
              <td><code>[kal̪-l̪aṁ]</code> — first <code>l</code> closes syllable</td>
              <td lang="pi"><strong>kalyā</strong> (กัลยา)</td>
              <td><code>[ka-l̪jaː]</code> — <code>ly</code> forms a cluster onset</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td lang="pi"><strong>akkhittā</strong> (อักขิต์ตา)</td>
              <td><code>[ak-kʰit̪-t̪aː]</code> — geminate stops</td>
              <td lang="pi"><strong>hitvā</strong> (หิตวา)</td>
              <td><code>[ɦi-t̪ʋaː]</code> — <code>tv</code> forms a cluster onset</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td lang="pi"><strong>mettā</strong> (เมต์ตา)</td>
              <td><code>[met̪-t̪aː]</code> — short <code>e</code> before geminate <code>tt</code></td>
              <td lang="pi"><strong>petvā</strong> (เปตวา)</td>
              <td><code>[peː-t̪ʋaː]</code> — long <code>eː</code> before cluster <code>tv</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td lang="pi"><strong>bhoggo</strong> (โภค์โค)</td>
              <td><code>[bʱog-goː]</code> — short <code>o</code> before geminate <code>gg</code></td>
              <td lang="pi"><strong>ārogyā</strong> (อาโรคยา)</td>
              <td><code>[aː-roː-gjaː]</code> — long <code>oː</code> before cluster <code>gy</code></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </article>

